ukrainians have suffered immensely in  this war but it appears that the  conflict is not going well for russia's  forces by some estimates they've already  lost as many troops in 28 days as they  did in 10 years of war in afghanistan  holly williams is about 100 miles west  of the capital kiev holly good morning  good morning we were here when russia  launched its first missiles and  airstrikes a month ago today but instead  of a lightning invasion russian forces  appear to have stalled with ukraine  claiming it's killed six russian  generals and even destroyed a russian  navy ship this morning the human cost of  this war though is horrifying  if vladimir putin thought he'd score an  easy victory in ukraine he knows better  now  in just one month between seven and  fifteen thousand russian soldiers have  been killed according to a nato official  the ukrainians are still out gunned yet  in some places they're clawing back  territory from the invaders but the cost  of this brutal invasion is being paid in  the lives of civilians the besieged city  of mariopol has been laid to waste by  putin's forces with more than a hundred  thousand people still thought to be  trapped inside  fifteen-year-old masha made it out of  mario pole but had her right leg  amputated after it was torn apart in a  russian strike  her doctor says she's so traumatized she  couldn't eat for days it breaks my heart  hearts of all ukrainians and every free  person on the planet in a video message  last night ukraine's president vladimir  zelensky accused russia of trying to  wipe ukrainians off the face of the  earth  this is only the beginning for russia on  the ukrainian land  in the city of jittermeir sergei is  sifting through the wreckage of his home  he spent 12 years building it for his  family he told us but russian airstrikes  destroyed it earlier this month killing  four in his neighborhood one of them was  sergei's daughter katja who's left  behind a one-year-old daughter  i wish i'd died in her place  the pain doesn't go away  who do you blame  for this  of course i blame putin he said if i had  him in my hands i'd butcher him like a  goat  sir hey says he'll raise his  granddaughter and like other ukrainians  he's determined to rebuild  in the shattered city of harkiv this  week a cellist played in the rubble  creating beauty even amid the terror of  this ugly war  this is a country where the will to  survive and fight for freedom at any  cost is simply staggering  [Music]  in that video message president  zielenski called on people all over the  world to protest against russia's  invasion and he said that ukraine has  not received the aircraft and modern air  defense systems that it wants from its  allies  vlad holly my heart simply breaks for  sir hey and his family and all  ukrainians who are suffering through  this thank you for your reporting we  appreciate it
 

